    "correctAnswerText": "Cephalosporins",
    "explanation": "Hormones\n• Hormones with major influences on the immune system (mainly immunosuppressive)\n◦ Corticosteroids\n◦ Growth hormones\n◦ Vasopressin\n◦ Catecholamines\n“Stress Response” in Critical Illness\n• Increased release of mediators from the hypothalamus and pituitary (i.e., Prolactin, ACTH)\n• Supports BP and mobilizationof immune system\n• Prolonged response leads to immunosuppression\nNeuroendocrine/Immune Failure\n• Loss of normal pulsatile release – ACTH, Growth Hormone, TSH, prolactin, LH\n• Results in impaired ability to use fatty acids resulting in a tendency to store fat and use protein from muscle and organs\n• Impaired lymphocyte and monocyte function; increased apoptosis",
