    "scenario": "A 16-year-old female, with a BMI of 36, has been taking tetracycline for several months for acne and is now brought in for headache and vomiting. Papilledema is noted on physical examination. Her lumbar puncture reveals an opening pressure of 400 mmHg, and CSF analysis is normal. Brain CT scan reveals small-normal sized ventricles. Of the following, the most likely diagnosis is:",
