    "explanation": "Which Tests\n• Categorical →\n◦ Chi-square (X2)\n• Compares observed to expected values for each cell\n• Can be used for >2 groups and unpaired data\n◦ Fisher’s exact\n• Used for unpaired data and smaller sample size (expected frequency of a cell is ≤5)\n◦ McNemar’s Test\n• Equivalent of chi-square test, but for paired data\nWhich Tests to Use? Categorical\n• Chi-square\n◦ Categorical (nominal) data\n◦ Unpaired (independent) observations\n◦ Two or >2 groups compared\n• T-test\n◦ Continuous data\n◦ Parametric (normal, bell-shaped distribution)\n◦ Unpaired (independent) observations\n◦ Two groups compared\nNormal vs Skewed Distributions",
