    "scenario": "A researcher has randomly selected two large groups from a population of children with asthma and would like to study the effect of a new therapy on the FEV1/FVC percentage. She finds that the frequency of the values of the FEV1/FVC percentage in each group has a bell-shaped distribution and that the variances are not distinguishable. To make sure that the samples do not differ significantly in their initial mean FEV1/FVC values, she plans to estimate the probability that the two means for the FEV1/FVC percentage are the same. The most appropriate test to measure the statistical significance between these two groups would be:",
