    "scenario": "A 7 y.o. male patient with a h/o congestive heart failure (CHF) secondary to dilated cardiomyopathy is admitted to PICU after exploratory laparotomy for ruptured appendix and peritonitis. Preoperatively he was receiving digoxin, furosemide and captopril 3 times a day for CHF treatment. On admission he is mechanically ventilated and receiving NS infusion at 11/2 maintenance and epinephrine infusion. On admission electrolytes are obtained: Na 135 mMol/L, K 2.5 mMol/L, Mg 1.2 mg/dL. Hypokalemia can be exacerbated by each of the following EXCEPT:",
