    "explanation": "Sedation\n• Medical management\n◦ Prevent loss of monitoring lines, vascular access, and airway\n◦ Facilitate management of severe lung disease (ARDS, asthma) or e.g. post- op care after airway reconstruction surgery\n◦ Facilitate control of ICP\n◦ Improvement of patient-ventilator dyssynchrony\n• Pain control\n• Palliative care/terminal sedation\n• Tolerance to hypnosedative drugs occurs during long-term (>24 hr) sedation\n◦ Indicated by the need for escalating doses or infusion rates of drugs to maintain same goal effect\n◦ Tolerance over a period of hours =\nTachyphylaxis\n• Seen most commonly with propofol\n• Tolerance requires tapering doses before drugs can be withdrawn completely",
    "source": "American Physician Institute 2012-2020",
    "category": "American Physician Institute 2012-2020 - Management of Pain and Sedation in the Intensive Care Unit (ICU)"
