    "explanation": "Module: Anemia\nOverview\n• 2 SD below normal value for age\n• Better tolerated in children (increased\n2,3DPG)\n• Most children (about 70%) in the PICU have anemia (arrive with it or develop it)\n• Compensation mechanisms also include increased cardiac output, re-distribution of capillary blood flow, increase production and decreased destruction or RBC’s\n◦ Increased production (erythropoietin) may be decreased in critical illness\n• Adjusted reticulocyte count <2% suggests decreased production",
    "source": "American Physician Institute 2012-2020",
    "category": "American Physician Institute 2012-2020 - Anemia"
