    "correctAnswerText": "Restrictive red blood cell transfusion practices are beneficial for critically ill children",
    "explanation": "Mechanisms\n• Clinical diagnosis (no diagnostic test available)\n• Antibody induced non-cardiogenic lung edema\nTRALI: Diagnosis\n• Suspected TRALI: case meets criteria and no other risk factor for acute lung injury\n• Possible TRALI: another risk factor for acute lung injury present\n• Delayed TRALI: onset within 6-72 hours of blood transfusion\n• Patients with sepsis may be at increased risk\n• Transfusion associated circulatory overload (TACO): normal or decreased LV function, increased PA occlusion pressure, elevated BNP\nModule: Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation",
