    "title": "You are conducting rounds at 10 a.m. on a 12 y.o. who was involved in a motor-vehicle collision and who has developed acute respir",
    "scenario": "You are conducting rounds at 10 a.m. on a 12 y.o. who was involved in a motor-vehicle collision and who has developed acute respiratory failure. The fellow states that conventional mechanical ventilation was initiated at 5 a.m. this morning and that he believes the patient’s condition has deteriorated. Arterial blood gas analysis show: pH 7.34, PaO2 53 torr on FiO2 0.70 and a PaCO2 59 torr. You see that the end-tidal CO2 reading on the monitor is 31 mmHg. One of the medical students who is attending the rounds asks you: “what is the reason for the CO2 retention in this patient? You should state that it is due to:",
